        <div class="my-4 col-11 m-auto">
            <!-- Article Content -->
            <div class="article-content redesign-text fr-view">
    <p><p style='margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:15px;font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;margin:0in;margin-bottom:16.8pt;background:white;' data-pasted="true"><span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">Early voting for the Massachusetts State Election begins Saturday, October 17 at Town Hall and absentee voting is already under way. <a href="https://www.northreadingma.gov/DocumentCenter/View/7837/11-3-26-State-election-ballotSAMPLE" target="_blank"><span style="color:#3A58A0;">This year&rsquo;s election ballot</span></a> includes a local ballot question for a project to remove and replace the modular classrooms at the J. Turner Hood and E. Ethel Little Schools.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">At <a href="https://www.northreadingma.gov/m/newsflash/home/detail/143" target="_blank"><span style="color:#3A58A0;">October 2026 Town Meeting</span></a>, North Reading voters appropriated $3,500,000.00 to remove and replace modular classrooms at Hood and Little Schools, to be bonded contingent on approval of Proposition 2 1/2 Debt Exclusion. </span>For additional information on the project,<span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;"><span style="color:#3A58A0;">&nbsp;</span></span><span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;"><a href="https://www.northreadingma.gov/DocumentCenter/View/7844/OTM-2026-Presentation-Article-12" target="_blank"><span style="color:#3A58A0;">please see Article 12 information presented at Town Meeting</span></a> and&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;"><a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1saJxWdp8JeRGDH8BFDqbKdETImQYkrZS/view" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Modular Classroom Replacement Rough Order of Magnitude pricing (ROM) Proposal</a></span><span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">. Video of the meeting presentation can also be found on the <a href="https://youtu.be/vYx8OoHnl88?list=PL33g5eS4dXJIrVOkw21wEkycYNV4wIzID&t=2722" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span style="color:#3A58A0;">NORCAM youtube channel</span></a>, at approximately 45:25 minutes.</span></p><p style='margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:15px;font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;margin:0in;margin-bottom:16.8pt;background:white;'><span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">The anticipated annual impact on the tax rate:</span></p><p style='margin-right:0in;margin-left:.25in;font-size:15px;font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;margin:0in;margin-bottom:4.2pt;background:white;'><span style='font-size:13px;font-family:"Courier New";color:#0A090C;'>o</span> <span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">For level debt service, based on FY 2026 rates, impact is projected to be $0.06 per $1,000 of valuation ($52.96 for average single family home valued at $883,502)</span></p><p style='margin-right:0in;margin-left:.25in;font-size:15px;font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;margin:0in;margin-bottom:4.2pt;background:white;'><span style='font-size:13px;font-family:"Courier New";color:#0A090C;'>o</span> <span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">For declining debt service, based on FY 2026 rates, impact is projected to range from $0.07 per $1,000 of valuation ($62.88 for average single family home valued at $883,502) declining to $0.05 per $1,000 of valuation ($39.84 for average single family home valued at $883,502)</span></p><p style='margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:15px;font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;margin:0in;margin-bottom:16.8pt;background:white;'><span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">Proposition 2 &frac12; is a state law that caps the overall property tax &ldquo;levy limit&rdquo; on existing property to 2 &frac12; percent increases per year, plus tax revenue from new growth that adds to the town&rsquo;s tax base. Question 10 proposes to temporarily increase property taxes above the amounts otherwise allowed under Proposition 2 &frac12;. The increase is for the amount of the annual debt service payments for the approved project, and it lasts only for the life of the related borrowing.</span></p><p style='margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:15px;font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;margin:0in;margin-bottom:16.8pt;background:white;'><span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">The Massachusetts Division of Local Services offers <a href="https://www.mass.gov/info-details/proposition-2-12-and-tax-rate-process" target="_blank"><span style="color:#3A58A0;">short video clips explaining Proposition 2 &frac12;</span></a></span></p><h2 style='margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:24px;font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;font-weight:bold;margin-bottom:.0001pt;background:white;'><strong><span style="font-size:21px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">QUESTION 10</span></strong></h2><p style='margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:15px;font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;margin:0in;margin-bottom:16.8pt;background:white;'><span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">Shall the Town of North Reading be allowed to exempt from the provisions of proposition two and one-half, so-called, the amounts required to pay for the bond issued in order to remove and replace the modular classrooms at the J. Turner Hood and E. Ethel Little Schools?</span></p><p style='margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:15px;font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;margin:0in;margin-bottom:16.8pt;background:white;'><strong><span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">A YES VOTE</span></strong><span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">&nbsp;would mean the project will proceed as approved at Town Meeting and classroom space needs will be addressed.</span></p><p style='margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:15px;font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;margin:0in;margin-bottom:16.8pt;background:white;'><strong><span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">A NO VOTE </span></strong><span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">would mean the project will not proceed, the School Committee will continue to operate with existing s</span><span style="font-size:14px;font-family:Lato;color:#0A090C;">pace, and incur maintenance costs for the existing modulars until another funding source is identified.</span></p></p>
</div>



            <hr class="my-4"/>

            <!-- Article Footer / Related News -->
            
	<div class="article-footer articles-category">
		<h2 id="related-articles-header" class="mb-0 fs-4">Related News</h2>
		<ul aria-labelledby="related-articles-header" id="list-related-category-5" class="list-group list-group-flush ps-0">
				<li class="list-group-item px-0 py-3 mx-2 bg-transparent">
					<div class="border-article article-link ps-2">
						<div>
							<h3 class="fs-6 title-truncate title-truncate-2">
									<a href="/m/newsflash/Home/Detail/152" class="article-title-link"
									   hx-get="/m/newsflash/Home/Detail/152"
									   hx-trigger="click"
									   hx-target="#outer-wrapper"
									   hx-swap="innerHTML show:window:top"
									   hx-push-url="true"
